      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Homeowners insurance in Utah covers a roof leak only if it is caused by a sudden, accidental covered peril\u2014such as a severe windstorm, hailstorm, heavy snow/ice weight, falling tree, or fire.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Inspect and Document: Take clear photos and videos of the active leak, interior damage, and any visible exterior or storm damage immediately."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Mitigate Further Damage: Take reasonable steps (like placing a tarp or bucket) to prevent more water from entering, as failing to mitigate can jeopardize a claim."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Check Your Policy: Review your deductible, coverage limits, and any specific Utah wind/hail exclusions before calling your insurer. You can also consult resources from the Utah Insurance Department .",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
                "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/home-insurance/home-claims-info/"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              2,
              3,
              8,
              9
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like to share:"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can give you more specific guidance on how claims typically handle your situation."
      }
